From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wbemprox: Win32_Environment, Win32_StartupCommand, Win32_TimeZone; a class with no instance is still a class

Win32_Environment lists the machine's variables (<SYSTEM>) and the user's, as stored (REG_EXPAND_SZ unexpanded), with Caption "owner\name"; Win32_StartupCommand lists the HKLM and HKCU Run keys (Location HKU\<sid>\... for the user's) and the Startup folders (Common Startup and Startup); Win32_TimeZone is GetTimeZoneInformation with the registry's display name. GetObject of a class that has no instance returns the class (__GENUS 1, class-level __PATH and __RELPATH, properties without values) instead of "not found", so scripts and wmic see "No Instance(s) Available." for an empty class. Properties read back from a spawned instance carry the plain CIM type, not the column's flags.
